# Paths other AI CLIs should not walk.
#
# KEEP THIS FILE AND .qwenignore IDENTICAL — same content under two names, because
# each tool looks only for its own filename. There is no include mechanism to share
# them, so a change here is a change there.
#
# Entries are here for one of two reasons:
#   SIZE        — these trees run to 100k+ files and, for activations/, ~126 GB.
#                 Walking them is slow and yields nothing readable.
#   SENSITIVITY — data/user_dumps/ holds real users' localStorage exports, each
#                 carrying an account credential (the userId IS the password) and a
#                 full answer history. Never send it to a third-party service.
#                 See data/README.md.

# Generated corpus and model artifacts (all regenerable — .gitignore says how)
activations/
tsumegos/
axes/
attempts/
ratings/
models/
pwa/tsumegos/
pwa/dist/

# Local snapshot of the production database
db/

# Real user data — read data/README.md before touching
data/user_dumps/

# Dependencies and local runtime state
.venv/
node_modules/
.wrangler/
